"field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "8"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13953040/state.json" "file_sha256" "ce6fd9130710f6f82288974366e6ed398a205420c8d0ca28f3d611f8be15c012" "basis" 615 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13953040/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-115105" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13953040/state.json" "file_sha256" "ce6fd9130710f6f82288974366e6ed398a205420c8d0ca28f3d611f8be15c012" "basis" 615 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13953040/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-51141" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that \n\n$$\n\\frac{2x+6}{(x-1)^{2}(x+1)}=\\frac{A}{x-1}+\\frac{B}{(x-1)^{2}}+\\frac{C}{x+1},\n$$\n\nwhere $A$, $B$, and $C$ are real constants, determine the value of $A\\cdot B\\cdot C.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13953040/state.json" "file_sha256" "ce6fd9130710f6f82288974366e6ed398a205420c8d0ca28f3d611f8be15c012" "basis" 615 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13953040/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-51141" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Multiplying both sides of the given equality by $(x-1)^{2}(x+1)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+6=A(x-1)(x+1)+B(x+1)+C(x-1)^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=-1$  gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(-1)+6 & =A(-1-1)(-1+1)+B(-1+1)+C(-1-1)^{2} \\\\ 4 & =4C \\\\ C & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=1$  gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(1)+6 & =A(1-1)(1+1)+B(1+1)+C(1-1)^{2} \\\\ 8 & =2B \\\\ B & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, letting $x=0$ and using our values for $B$ and $C$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(0)+6 & =A(0-1)(0+1)+4(0+1)+1(0-1)^{2} \\\\ 6 & =-A+4+1 \\\\ A & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nHence,\n\n$$\nA\\cdot B\\cdot C=(-1)\\cdot 4\\cdot 1=-4.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13953040/state.json" "file_sha256" "ce6fd9130710f6f82288974366e6ed398a205420c8d0ca28f3d611f8be15c012" "basis" 615 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13953040/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-51141" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13953040/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "66b1124bc06eaefc8dee48c0246afb3d6799036270ec7eb9de3f06955de9e220" "basis" 615 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13953040/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-51141" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13953040/state.json" "file_sha256" "ce6fd9130710f6f82288974366e6ed398a205420c8d0ca28f3d611f8be15c012" "basis" 615 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13953040/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-51141" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-10"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13953040/state.json" "file_sha256" "ce6fd9130710f6f82288974366e6ed398a205420c8d0ca28f3d611f8be15c012" "basis" 615 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13953040/edb-import/verification.j