ed}x-4 & =A(x-2)-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=0$  gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0-4 & =A(0-2)-2 \\\\ -4 & =-2A-2 \\\\ 2A & =2 \\\\ A & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/state.json" "file_sha256" "a214c7f56d4a405e541980213466c5f921d158e09d5c1a7b15833d74a3eb6b65"} {"question" "q-73206" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0cc918ffd366d63cb92a1aec3422bc69dfe141ce7f8b052fa946427f57512019"} {"question" "q-73206" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/state.json" "file_sha256" "a214c7f56d4a405e541980213466c5f921d158e09d5c1a7b15833d74a3eb6b65"} {"question" "q-73206" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-2"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "2"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/state.json" "file_sha256" "a214c7f56d4a405e541980213466c5f921d158e09d5c1a7b15833d74a3eb6b65"} {"question" "q-73206" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/state.json" "file_sha256" "a214c7f56d4a405e541980213466c5f921d158e09d5c1a7b15833d74a3eb6b65"} {"question" "q-115113" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that \n\n$$\n\\frac{7x+20}{(x+4)^{2}}=\\frac{A}{x+4}+\\frac{B}{(x+4)^{2}},\n$$\n\nfind the real constants $A$ and $B.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/state.json" "file_sha256" "a214c7f56d4a405e541980213466c5f921d158e09d5c1a7b15833d74a3eb6b65"} {"question" "q-115113" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Multiplying both sides of the given equality by $(x+4)^{2}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7x+20 & =A(x+4)+B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=-4$  gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7(-4)+20 & =A(-4+4)+B \\\\ -8 & =B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=0$ and using our value for $B$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7(0)+20 & =A(0+4)-8 \\\\ 20 & =4A-8 \\\\ 28 & =4A \\\\ A & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $A=7$ and $B=-8.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/state.json" "file_sha256" "a214c7f56d4a405e541980213466c5f921d158e09d5c1a7b15833d74a3eb6b65"} {"question" "q-115113" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0cc918ffd366d63cb92a1aec3422bc69dfe141ce7f8b052fa946427f57512019"} {"question" "q-115113" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/state.json" "file_sha256" "a214c7f56d4a405e541980213466c5f921d158e09d5c1a7b15833d74a3eb6b65"} {"question" "q-115113" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$A=-4$ and $B=-8$"] ["text" "$A=-7$ and $B=-6$"] ["text" "$A=4$ and $B=5$"] ["text" "$A=7$ and $B=-8$"] ["text" "$A=7$ and $B=6$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/state.json" "file_sha256" "a214c7f56d4a405e541980213466c5f921d158e09d5c1a7b15833d74a3eb6b65"} {"question" "q-115113" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$A=7$ and $B=-8$"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/state.json" "file_sha256" "a214c7f56d4a405e541980213466c5f921d158e09d5c1a7b15833d74a3eb6b65"} {"question" "q-73204" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that \n\n$$\n\\frac{x+8}{(x-2)^{2}}=\\frac{A}{x-2}+\\frac{B}{(x-2)^{2}},\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ and $B$ are real constants, what is the value of $A\\cdot B?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/state.json" "file_sha256" "a214c7f56d4a405e541980213466c5f921d158e09d5c1a7b15833d74a3eb6b65"} {"question" "q-73204" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Multiplying both sides of the given equality by $(x-2)^{2}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+8 & =A(x-2)+B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=2$  gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2+8 & =A(2-2)+B \\\\ 10 & =B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=0$ and using our value for $B$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0+8 & =A(0-2)+10 \\\\ -2 & =-2A \\\\ A & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nA\\cdot B=1\\cdot 10=10.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/state.json" "file_sha256" "a214c7f56d4a405e541980213466c5f921d158e09d5c1a7b15833d74a3eb6b65"} {"question" "q-73204" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0cc918ffd366d63cb92a1aec3422bc69dfe141ce7f8b052fa946427f57512019"} {"question" "q-73204" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/state.json" "file_sha256" "a214c7f56d4a405e541980213466c5f921d158e09d5c1a7b15833d74a3eb6b65"} {"question" "q-73204" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "10"] ["math" "11"] ["math" "12"] ["math" "8"] ["math" "9"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/state.json" "file_sha256" "a214c7f56d4a405e541980213466c5f921d158e09d5c1a7b15833d74a3eb6b65"} {"question" "q-73204" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "10"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/state.json" "file_sha256" "a214c7f56d4a405e541980213466c5f921d158e09d5c1a7b15833d74a3eb6b65"} {"question" "q-115117" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that \n\n$$\n\\frac{x+1}{(x+5)^{2}}=\\frac{A}{x+5}+\\frac{B}{(x+5)^{2}},\n$$\n\nfind the real constants $A$ and $B.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/state.json" "file_sha256" "a214c7f56d4a405e541980213466c5f921d158e09d5c1a7b15833d74a3eb6b65"} {"question" "q-115117" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Multiplying both sides of the given equality by $(x+5)^{2}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+1 & =A(x+5)+B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=-5$  gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-5+1 & =A(-5+5)+B \\\\ B & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=0$ and using our value for $B$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0+1 & =A(0+5)-4 \\\\ 1 & =5A-4 \\\\ 5 & =5A \\\\ A & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $A=1$ and $B=-4.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/state.json" "file_sha256" "a214c7f56d4a405e541980213466c5f921d158e09d5c1a7b15833d74a3eb6b65"} {"question" "q-115117" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0cc918ffd366d63cb92a1aec3422bc69dfe141ce7f8b052fa946427f57512019"} {"question" "q-115117" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/state.json" "file_sha256" "a214c7f56d4a405e541980213466c5f921d158e09d5c1a7b15833d74a3eb6b65"} {"question" "q-115117" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$A=-1$ and $B=2$"] ["text" "$A=-2$ and $B=-4$"] ["text" "$A=1$ and $B=-4$"] ["text" "$A=1$ and $B=6$"] ["text" "$A=2$ and $B=-6$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/state.json" "file_sha256" "a214c7f56d4a405e541980213466c5f921d158e09d5c1a7b15833d74a3eb6b65"} {"question" "q-115117" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$A=1$ and $B=-4$"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/state.json" "file_sha256" "a214c7f56d4a405e541980213466c5f921d158e09d5c1a7b15833d74a3eb6b65"} {"question" "q-115119" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that \n\n$$\n\\frac{-2x-1}{(x-1)^{2}}=\\frac{A}{x-1}+\\frac{B}{(x-1)^{2}},\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ and $B$ are real constants, what is the value of $A\\cdot B?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/state.json" "file_sha256" "a214c7f56d4a405e541980213466c5f921d158e09d5c1a7b15833d74a3eb6b65"} {"question" "q-115119" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Multiplying both sides of the given equality by $(x-1)^{2}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2x-1 & =A(x-1)+B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=1$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2(1)-1 & =A(1-1)+B \\\\ -3 & =B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=0$ and using our value for $B$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2(0)-1 & =A(0-1)-3 \\\\ -1 & =-A-3 \\\\ -A & =2 \\\\ A & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nA\\cdot B=(-2)\\cdot (-3)=6.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/state.json" "file_sha256" "a214c7f56d4a405e541980213466c5f921d158e09d5c1a7b15833d74a3eb6b65"} {"question" "q-115119" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0cc918ffd366d63cb92a1aec3422bc69dfe141ce7f8b052fa946427f57512019"} {"question" "q-115119" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/state.json" "file_sha256" "a214c7f56d4a405e541980213466c5f921d158e09d5c1a7b15833d74a3eb6b65"} {"question" "q-115119" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-6"] ["math" "-9"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "6"] ["math" "9"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/state.json" "file_sha256" "a214c7f56d4a405e541980213466c5f921d158e09d5c1a7b15833d74a3eb6b65"} {"question" "q-115119" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "6"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/state.json" "file_sha256" "a214c7f56d4a405e541980213466c5f921d158e09d5c1a7b15833d74a3eb6b65"} {"question" "q-351195" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Express $\\frac{7x+2}{(x+5)^{2}}$ as a sum of partial fractions.\n\n| $\\frac{7x+2}{(x+5)^{2}}=$ | {{field-1}} | $-$ | {{field-2}} |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $x+5$ |  | $(x+5)^{2}$ |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/state.json" "file_sha256" "a214c7f56d4a405e541980213466c5f921d158e09d5c1a7b15833d74a3eb6b65"} {"question" "q-351195" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Our task is to find $A$ and $B$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7x+2}{(x+5)^{2}}=\\frac{A}{x+5}+\\frac{B}{(x+5)^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the above equality by $(x+5)^{2}$ gives\n\n$$\n7x+2=A(x+5)+B.\n$$\n\nLetting $x=-5$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7(-5)+2 & =A(-5+5)+B \\\\ B & =-33.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=0$ and using our value for $B$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0+2 & =A(0+5)-33 \\\\ 2 & =5A-33 \\\\ A & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\frac{7x+2}{(x+5)^{2}}=\\frac{7}{x+5}-\\frac{33}{(x+5)^{2}}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/state.json" "file_sha256" "a214c7f56d4a405e541980213466c5f921d158e09d5c1a7b15833d74a3eb6b65"} {"question" "q-351195" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0cc918ffd366d63cb92a1aec3422bc69dfe141ce7f8b052fa946427f57512019"} {"question" "q-351195" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/state.json" "file_sha256" "a214c7f56d4a405e541980213466c5f921d158e09d5c1a7b15833d74a3eb6b65"} {"question" "q-351195" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "7"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/state.json" "file_sha256" "a214c7f56d4a405e541980213466c5f921d158e09d5c1a7b15833d74a3eb6b65"} {"question" "q-351195" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/state.json" "file_sha256" "a214c7f56d4a405e541980213466c5f921d158e09d5c1a7b15833d74a3eb6b65"} {"question" "q-351195" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "33"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/state.json" "file_sha256" "a214c7f56d4a405e541980213466c5f921d158e09d5c1a7b15833d74a3eb6b65"} {"question" "q-346820" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Express $\\frac{6{x}^{2}+x-3}{{x}^{2}(x-1)}$ as a sum of partial fractions.\n\n| $\\frac{6{x}^{2}+x-3}{{x}^{2}(x-1)}\\,=$ | {{field-1}} | $+$ | {{field-2}} | $+$ | {{field-3}} |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $x$ |  | ${x}^{2}$ |  | $x-1$ |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/state.json" "file_sha256" "a214c7f56d4a405e541980213466c5f921d158e09d5c1a7b15833d74a3eb6b65"} {"question" "q-346820" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Our task is to find $A,$ $B,$ and $C$ such that\n\n$$\n\\frac{6{x}^{2}+x-3}{{x}^{2}(x-1)}=\\frac{A}{x}+\\frac{B}{{x}^{2}}+\\frac{C}{x-1}.\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by ${x}^{2}(x-1)$ gives\n\n$$\n6{x}^{2}+x-3=Ax(x-1)+B(x-1)+C{x}^{2}.\n$$\n\nLetting $x=0$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6(0)^{2}+(0)-3 & =A(0)(0-1)+B(0-1)+C(0)^{2} \\\\ -3 & =B(-1) \\\\ B & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=1$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6(1)^{2}+(1)-3 & =A(1)(1-1)+B(1-1)+C(1)^{2} \\\\ 4 & =C(1)^{2} \\\\ 4 & =1C \\\\ C & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, letting $x=2$ and using our values for $B$ and $C$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6(2)^{2}+(2)-3 & =A(2)(2-1)+3(2-1)+4(2)^{2} \\\\ 23 & =A(2)(1)+3(1)+4(4) \\\\ 23 & =2A+3+16 \\\\ 23 & =2A+19 \\\\ A & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\frac{6{x}^{2}+x-3}{{x}^{2}(x-1)}=\\frac{2}{x}+\\frac{3}{{x}^{2}}+\\frac{4}{x-1}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/state.json" "file_sha256" "a214c7f56d4a405e541980213466c5f921d158e09d5c1a7b15833d74a3eb6b65"} {"question" "q-346820" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0cc918ffd366d63cb92a1aec3422bc69dfe141ce7f8b052fa946427f57512019"} {"question" "q-346820" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/state.json" "file_sha256" "a214c7f56d4a405e541980213466c5f921d158e09d5c1a7b15833d74a3eb6b65"} {"question" "q-346820" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/state.json" "file_sha256" "a214c7f56d4a405e541980213466c5f921d158e09d5c1a7b15833d74a3eb6b65"} {"question" "q-346820" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/state.json" "file_sha256" "a214c7f56d4a405e541980213466c5f921d158e09d5c1a7b15833d74a3eb6b65"} {"question" "q-346820" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/state.json" "file_sha256" "a214c7f56d4a405e541980213466c5f921d158e09d5c1a7b15833d74a3eb6b65"} {"question" "q-346820" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/state.json" "file_sha256" "a214c7f56d4a405e541980213466c5f921d158e09d5c1a7b15833d74a3eb6b65"} {"question" "q-346820" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/state.json" "file_sha256" "a214c7f56d4a405e541980213466c5f921d158e09d5c1a7b15833d74a3eb6b65"} {"question" "q-351226" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Express $\\frac{-22{x}^{2}+60x-26}{(x+1)(2x-4)^{2}}$ as a sum of partial fractions.\n\n| $\\frac{-22{x}^{2}+60x-26}{(x+1)(2x-4)^{2}}=$ | $-$ | {{field-1}} | $-$ | {{field-2}} | $+$ | {{field-3}} |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | $x+1$ |  | $2x-4$ |  | $(2x-4)^{2}$ |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/state.json" "file_sha256" "a214c7f56d4a405e541980213466c5f921d158e09d5c1a7b15833d74a3eb6b65"} {"question" "q-351226" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Our task is to find $A,$ $B,$ and $C$ such that\n\n$$\n\\frac{-22{x}^{2}+60x-26}{(x+1)(2x-4)^{2}}=\\frac{A}{x+1}+\\frac{B}{2x-4}+\\frac{C}{(2x-4)^{2}}.\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $(x+1)(2x-4)^{2}$ gives\n\n$$\n-22{x}^{2}+60x-26=A(2x-4)^{2}+B(x+1)(2x-4)+C(x+1).\n$$\n\nLetting $x=-1$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-22(-1)^{2}+60(-1)-26 & =A(2(-1)-4)^{2}+B(-1+1)(2(-1)-4)+C(-1+1) \\\\ -108 & =A(-6)^{2} \\\\ A & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=2$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-22(2)^{2}+60(2)-26 & =A(2\\cdot 2-4)^{2}+B(2+1)(2\\cdot 2-4)+C(2+1) \\\\ 6 & =C(3) \\\\ C & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, letting $x=0$ and using our values for $A$ and $C$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-22(0)^{2}+60(0)-26 & =A(2\\cdot 0-4)^{2}+B(0+1)(2\\cdot 0-4)+2(0+1) \\\\ -26 & =(-3)(16)+B(1)(-4)+2 \\\\ -26 & =-46-4B \\\\ B & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{-22{x}^{2}+60x-26}{(x+1)(2x-4)^{2}}=-\\,\\frac{3}{x+1}-\\,\\frac{5}{2x-4}+\\frac{2}{(2x-4)^{2}}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/state.json" "file_sha256" "a214c7f56d4a405e541980213466c5f921d158e09d5c1a7b15833d74a3eb6b65"} {"question" "q-351226" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0cc918ffd366d63cb92a1aec3422bc69dfe141ce7f8b052fa946427f57512019"} {"question" "q-351226" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/state.json" "file_sha256" "a214c7f56d4a405e541980213466c5f921d158e09d5c1a7b15833d74a3eb6b65"} {"question" "q-351226" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/state.json" "file_sha256" "a214c7f56d4a405e541980213466c5f921d158e09d5c1a7b15833d74a3eb6b65"} {"question" "q-351226" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/state.json" "file_sha256" "a214c7f56d4a405e541980213466c5f921d158e09d5c1a7b15833d74a3eb6b65"} {"question" "q-351226" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/state.json" "file_sha256" "a214c7f56d4a405e541980213466c5f921d158e09d5c1a7b15833d74a3eb6b65"} {"question" "q-351226" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/state.json" "file_sha256" "a214c7f56d4a405e541980213466c5f921d158e09d5c1a7b15833d74a3eb6b65"} {"question" "q-351226" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/state.json" "file_sha256" "a214c7f56d4a405e541980213466c5f921d158e09d5c1a7b15833d74a3eb6b65"} {"question" "q-51141" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that \n\n$$\n\\frac{2x+6}{(x-1)^{2}(x+1)}=\\frac{A}{x-1}+\\frac{B}{(x-1)^{2}}+\\frac{C}{x+1},\n$$\n\nwhere $A$, $B$, and $C$ are real constants, determine the value of $A\\cdot B\\cdot C.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/state.json" "file_sha256" "a214c7f56d4a405e541980213466c5f921d158e09d5c1a7b15833d74a3eb6b65"} {"question" "q-51141" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Multiplying both sides of the given equality by $(x-1)^{2}(x+1)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+6=A(x-1)(x+1)+B(x+1)+C(x-1)^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=-1$  gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(-1)+6 & =A(-1-1)(-1+1)+B(-1+1)+C(-1-1)^{2} \\\\ 4 & =4C \\\\ C & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=1$  gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(1)+6 & =A(1-1)(1+1)+B(1+1)+C(1-1)^{2} \\\\ 8 & =2B \\\\ B & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, letting $x=0$ and using our values for $B$ and $C$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(0)+6 & =A(0-1)(0+1)+4(0+1)+1(0-1)^{2} \\\\ 6 & =-A+4+1 \\\\ A & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nHence,\n\n$$\nA\\cdot B\\cdot C=(-1)\\cdot 4\\cdot 1=-4.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/state.json" "file_sha256" "a214c7f56d4a405e541980213466c5f921d158e09d5c1a7b15833d74a3eb6b65"} {"question" "q-51141" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0cc918ffd366d63cb92a1aec3422bc69dfe141ce7f8b052fa946427f57512019"} {"question" "q-51141" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/state.json" "file_sha256" "a214c7f56d4a405e541980213466c5f921d158e09d5c1a7b15833d74a3eb6b65"} {"question" "q-51141" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-10"] ["math" "-4"] ["math" "-8"] ["math" "15"] ["math" "9"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/state.json" "file_sha256" "a214c7f56d4a405e541980213466c5f921d158e09d5c1a7b15833d74a3eb6b65"} {"question" "q-51141" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/state.json" "file_sha256" "a214c7f56d4a405e541980213466c5f921d158e09d5c1a7b15833d74a3eb6b65"} {"question" "q-50049" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that \n\n$$\n\\frac{x+2}{{x}^{2}(2x+3)}=\\frac{A}{x}+\\frac{B}{{x}^{2}}+\\frac{C}{2x+3},\n$$\n\nwhere $A$, $B$, and $C$ are real constants, determine the value of $A\\cdot B\\cdot C.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/state.json" "file_sha256" "a214c7f56d4a405e541980213466c5f921d158e09d5c1a7b15833d74a3eb6b65"} {"question" "q-50049" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Multiplying both sides of the given equality by ${x}^{2}(2x+3)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+2 & =Ax(2x+3)+B(2x+3)+C{x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=0$  gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0+2 & =A(0)(2(0)+3)+B(2(0)+3)+C(0)^{2} \\\\ 2 & =3B \\\\ B & =\\frac{2}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=-\\frac{3}{2}$  gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{2}+2 & =A(-\\frac{3}{2})(2(-\\frac{3}{2})+3)+B(2(-\\frac{3}{2})+3)+C{(-\\frac{3}{2})}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & =C(\\frac{9}{4}) \\\\ C & =\\frac{4}{18} \\\\ C & =\\frac{2}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, letting $x=1$ and using our values for $B$ and $C$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1+2 & =A(1)(2(1)+3)+(\\frac{2}{3})(2(1)+3)+(\\frac{2}{9})(1)^{2} \\\\ 3 & =5A+\\frac{10}{3}+\\frac{2}{9} \\\\ 3 & =5A+\\frac{32}{9} \\\\ 5A & =-\\frac{5}{9} \\\\ A & =-\\frac{1}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A\\cdot B\\cdot C & =-\\frac{1}{9}\\cdot \\frac{2}{3}\\cdot \\frac{2}{9} \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{243}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/state.json" "file_sha256" "a214c7f56d4a405e541980213466c5f921d158e09d5c1a7b15833d74a3eb6b65"} {"question" "q-50049" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0cc918ffd366d63cb92a1aec3422bc69dfe141ce7f8b052fa946427f57512019"} {"question" "q-50049" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/state.json" "file_sha256" "a214c7f56d4a405e541980213466c5f921d158e09d5c1a7b15833d74a3eb6b65"} {"question" "q-50049" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{32}{75}"] ["math" "-\\frac{4}{243}"] ["math" "-\\frac{81}{256}"] ["math" "\\frac{27}{128}"] ["math" "\\frac{9}{125}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/state.json" "file_sha256" "a214c7f56d4a405e541980213466c5f921d158e09d5c1a7b15833d74a3eb6b65"} {"question" "q-50049" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{4}{243}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/state.json" "file_sha256" "a214c7f56d4a405e541980213466c5f921d158e09d5c1a7b15833d74a3eb6b65"} {"question" "q-51140" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that \n\n$$\n\\frac{4{x}^{2}-23x+27}{x(x-3)^{2}}=\\frac{A}{x}+\\frac{B}{x-3}+\\frac{C}{(x-3)^{2}},\n$$\n\nwhere $A$, $B$, and $C$ are real constants, determine the value of $A\\cdot B\\cdot C.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/state.json" "file_sha256" "a214c7f56d4a405e541980213466c5f921d158e09d5c1a7b15833d74a3eb6b65"} {"question" "q-51140" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Multiplying both sides of the given equality by $x(x-3)^{2}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{2}-23x+27=A(x-3)^{2}+Bx(x-3)+Cx.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=3$  gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(3)^{2}-23(3)+27 & =A(3-3)^{2}+B\\cdot 3(3-3)+C\\cdot 3 \\\\ 36-69+27 & =3C \\\\ -6 & =3C \\\\ C & =\\frac{(-6)}{3} \\\\ C & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=0$  gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(0)^{2}-23(0)+27 & =A(0-3)^{2}+B(0)(0-3)+C(0) \\\\ 27 & =9A \\\\ A & =\\frac{27}{9} \\\\ A & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, letting $x=1$ and using our values for $A$ and $C$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(1)^{2}-23(1)+27 & =3(1-3)^{2}+B(1)(1-3)+(-2)(1) \\\\ 4-23+27 & =12-2B-2 \\\\ 8 & =10-2B \\\\ 2B & =2 \\\\ B & =\\frac{2}{2} \\\\ B & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nHence,\n\n$$\nA\\cdot B\\cdot C=3\\cdot 1\\cdot (-2)=-6.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/state.json" "file_sha256" "a214c7f56d4a405e541980213466c5f921d158e09d5c1a7b15833d74a3eb6b65"} {"question" "q-51140" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0cc918ffd366d63cb92a1aec3422bc69dfe141ce7f8b052fa946427f57512019"} {"question" "q-51140" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/state.json" "file_sha256" "a214c7f56d4a405e541980213466c5f921d158e09d5c1a7b15833d74a3eb6b65"} {"question" "q-51140" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-4"] ["math" "-6"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "8"] ["math" "9"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/state.json" "file_sha256" "a214c7f56d4a405e541980213466c5f921d158e09d5c1a7b15833d74a3eb6b65"} {"question" "q-51140" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-6"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/state.json" "file_sha256" "a214c7f56d4a405e541980213466c5f921d158e09d5c1a7b15833d74a3eb6b65"} {"question" "q-346933" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Express $\\frac{2{x}^{2}-5x+9}{(x+2)^{3}}$ as a sum of partial fractions.\n\n| $\\frac{2{x}^{2}-5x+9}{(x+2)^{3}}\\,=$ | {{field-1}} | $-$ | {{field-2}} | $+$ | {{field-3}} |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $x+2$ |  | $(x+2)^{2}$ |  | $(x+2)^{3}$ |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/state.json" "file_sha256" "a214c7f56d4a405e541980213466c5f921d158e09d5c1a7b15833d74a3eb6b65"} {"question" "q-346933" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Our task is to find $A,$ $B,$ and $C$ such that\n\n$$\n\\frac{2{x}^{2}-5x+9}{(x+2)^{3}}=\\frac{A}{x+2}+\\frac{B}{(x+2)^{2}}+\\frac{C}{(x+2)^{3}}.\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $(x+2)^{3}$ gives\n\n$$\n2{x}^{2}-5x+9=A(x+2)^{2}+B(x+2)+C.\n$$\n\nLetting $x=-2$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(-2)^{2}-5(-2)+9 & =A(-2+2)^{2}+B(-2+2)+C \\\\ 27 & =A(0)^{2}+B(0)+C \\\\ C & =27.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=-1$ and using our value for $C$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(-1)^{2}-5(-1)+9 & =A(-1+2)^{2}+B(-1+2)+27 \\\\ 16 & =A+B+27 \\\\ B & =-A-11.\\,\\,(1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, letting $x=0$ and using our value for $C$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(0)^{2}-5(0)+9 & =A(0+2)^{2}+B(0+2)+27 \\\\ 9 & =4A+2B+27 \\\\ 2B & =-4A-18 \\\\ B & =-2A-9.\\,\\,(2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom $(1)$ and $(2)$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-A-11 & =-2A-9 \\\\ A & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we substitute the value of $A$ into $(1)$ to get the value of $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B & =-2-11 \\\\ B & =-13\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\frac{2{x}^{2}-5x+9}{(x+2)^{3}}=\\frac{2}{x+2}-\\frac{13}{(x+2)^{2}}+\\frac{27}{(x+2)^{3}}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/state.json" "file_sha256" "a214c7f56d4a405e541980213466c5f921d158e09d5c1a7b15833d74a3eb6b65"} {"question" "q-346933" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0cc918ffd366d63cb92a1aec3422bc69dfe141ce7f8b052fa946427f57512019"} {"question" "q-346933" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/state.json" "file_sha256" "a214c7f56d4a405e541980213466c5f921d158e09d5c1a7b15833d74a3eb6b65"} {"question" "q-346933" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/state.json" "file_sha256" "a214c7f56d4a405e541980213466c5f921d158e09d5c1a7b15833d74a3eb6b65"} {"question" "q-346933" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/state.json" "file_sha256" "a214c7f56d4a405e541980213466c5f921d158e09d5c1a7b15833d74a3eb6b65"} {"question" "q-346933" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "13"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/state.json" "file_sha256" "a214c7f56d4a405e541980213466c5f921d158e09d5c1a7b15833d74a3eb6b65"} {"question" "q-346933" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/state.json" "file_sha256" "a214c7f56d4a405e541980213466c5f921d158e09d5c1a7b15833d74a3eb6b65"} {"question" "q-346933" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "27"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/state.json" "file_sha256" "a214c7f56d4a405e541980213466c5f921d158e09d5c1a7b15833d74a3eb6b65"} {"question" "q-70014" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that\n\n$$\n\\frac{-{x}^{2}-3x-1}{x(x+1)^{3}}=\\frac{A}{x}+\\frac{B}{x+1}+\\frac{C}{(x+1)^{2}}+\\frac{D}{(x+1)^{3}},\n$$\n\nwhere $A$, $B$, $C$ and $D$ are real constants, determine the value of $AB-CD.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/state.json" "file_sha256" "a214c7f56d4a405e541980213466c5f921d158e09d5c1a7b15833d74a3eb6b65"} {"question" "q-70014" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Multiplying both sides of the given equality by $x(x+1)^{3}$ gives\n\n$$\n-{x}^{2}-3x-1=A(x+1)^{3}+Bx(x+1)^{2}+Cx(x+1)+Dx.\n$$\n\nLetting $x=-1$  gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-(-1)^{2}-3(-1)-1 & =A(-1+1)^{3}+B(-1)(-1+1)^{2}+C(-1)(-1+1)+D(-1) \\\\ -1+3-1 & =-D \\\\ 1 & =-D \\\\ D & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=0$  gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-(0)^{2}-3(0)-1 & =A(0+1)^{3}+B(0)(0+1)^{2}+C(0)(0+1)+D(0) \\\\ -1 & =A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=1$ and using our values for $A$ and $D$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-(1)^{2}-3(1)-1 & =(-1)(1+1)^{3}+B(1)(1+1)^{2}+C(1)(1+1)+(-1)(1) \\\\ -1-3-1 & =-8+4B+2C-1 \\\\ 2C & =4-4B \\\\ C & =2-2B.\\,\\,(1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, letting $x=2$ and using our values for $A$ and $D$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-(2)^{2}-3(2)-1 & =(-1)(2+1)^{3}+B(2)(2+1)^{2}+C(2)(2+1)+(-1)(2) \\\\ -4-6-1 & =-27+18B+6C-2 \\\\ 6C & =18-18B \\\\ C & =3-3B.\\,\\,(2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom $(1)$ and $(2)$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2-2B & =3-3B \\\\ B & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we substitute the value of $B$ into $(1)$ to get the value of $C:$\n\n$$\nC=2-2(1)=0\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\nAB-CD=(-1)(1)-0(-1)=-1.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/state.json" "file_sha256" "a214c7f56d4a405e541980213466c5f921d158e09d5c1a7b15833d74a3eb6b65"} {"question" "q-70014" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0cc918ffd366d63cb92a1aec3422bc69dfe141ce7f8b052fa946427f57512019"} {"question" "q-70014" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/state.json" "file_sha256" "a214c7f56d4a405e541980213466c5f921d158e09d5c1a7b15833d74a3eb6b65"} {"question" "q-70014" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-4"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "3"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/state.json" "file_sha256" "a214c7f56d4a405e541980213466c5f921d158e09d5c1a7b15833d74a3eb6b65"} {"question" "q-70014" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-1"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/state.json" "file_sha256" "a214c7f56d4a405e541980213466c5f921d158e09d5c1a7b15833d74a3eb6b65"} {"question" "q-115217" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that \n\n$$\n\\frac{3{x}^{2}-7x+8}{(x-1)^{3}}=\\frac{A}{x-1}+\\frac{B}{(x-1)^{2}}+\\frac{C}{(x-1)^{3}},\n$$\n\nwhere $A$, $B$ and $C$ are real constants, find the value of $A\\cdot B\\cdot C.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/state.json" "file_sha256" "a214c7f56d4a405e541980213466c5f921d158e09d5c1a7b15833d74a3eb6b65"} {"question" "q-115217" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Multiplying both sides of the given equality by $(x-1)^{3}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2}-7x+8 & =A(x-1)^{2}+B(x-1)+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=1$  gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(1)^{2}-7(1)+8 & =A(1-1)^{2}+B(1-1)+C \\\\ 4 & =A(0)+B(0)+C \\\\ C & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=0$ and using our value for $C$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(0)^{2}-7(0)+8 & =A(0-1)^{2}+B(0-1)+4 \\\\ 8 & =A-B+4 \\\\ 0 & =A-B-4 \\\\ B & =A-4.\\,\\,(1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, letting $x=2$ and using our value for $C$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(2)^{2}-7(2)+8 & =A(2-1)^{2}+B(2-1)+4 \\\\ 6 & =A+B+4 \\\\ 0 & =A+B-2 \\\\ B & =2-A.\\,\\,(2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom $(1)$ and $(2)$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-4 & =2-A \\\\ 2A & =6 \\\\ A & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we substitute the value of $A$ into $(2)$  to get the value of $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B & =3-4=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A\\cdot B\\cdot C & =3\\cdot (-1)\\cdot 4=-12.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/state.json" "file_sha256" "a214c7f56d4a405e541980213466c5f921d158e09d5c1a7b15833d74a3eb6b65"} {"question" "q-115217" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0cc918ffd366d63cb92a1aec3422bc69dfe141ce7f8b052fa946427f57512019"} {"question" "q-115217" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/state.json" "file_sha256" "a214c7f56d4a405e541980213466c5f921d158e09d5c1a7b15833d74a3eb6b65"} {"question" "q-115217" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-10"] ["math" "-12"] ["math" "15"] ["math" "6"] ["math" "8"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/state.json" "file_sha256" "a214c7f56d4a405e541980213466c5f921d158e09d5c1a7b15833d74a3eb6b65"} {"question" "q-115217" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-12"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/state.json" "file_sha256" "a214c7f56d4a405e541980213466c5f921d158e09d5c1a7b15833d74a3eb6b65"} {"question" "q-351243" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Express $\\frac{7{x}^{2}-32x+42}{(x-2)^{3}}$ as a sum of partial fractions.\n\n| $\\frac{7{x}^{2}-32x+42}{(x-2)^{3}}\\,=$ | {{field-1}} | $-$ | {{field-2}} | $+$ | {{field-3}} |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $x-2$ |  | $(x-2)^{2}$ |  | $(x-2)^{3}$ |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/state.json" "file_sha256" "a214c7f56d4a405e541980213466c5f921d158e09d5c1a7b15833d74a3eb6b65"} {"question" "q-351243" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Our task is to find $A,$ $B,$ and $C$ such that\n\n$$\n\\frac{7{x}^{2}-32x+42}{(x-2)^{3}}=\\frac{A}{x-2}+\\frac{B}{(x-2)^{2}}+\\frac{C}{(x-2)^{3}}.\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $(x-2)^{3}$ gives\n\n$$\n7{x}^{2}-32x+42=A(x-2)^{2}+B(x-2)+C.\n$$\n\nLetting $x=2$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7(2)^{2}-32(2)+42 & =A(2-2)^{2}+B(2-2)+C \\\\ 6 & =C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=3$ and using our value for $C$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7(3)^{2}-32(3)+42 & =A(3-2)^{2}+B(3-2)+6 \\\\ 9 & =A+B+6 \\\\ B & =3-A.\\,\\,(1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, letting $x=0$ and using our value for $C$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7(0)^{2}-32(0)+42 & =A(0-2)^{2}+B(0-2)+6 \\\\ 42 & =4A-2B+6 \\\\ 36 & =4A-2B \\\\ B & =2A-18.\\,\\,(2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom $(1)$ and $(2)$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3-A & =2A-18 \\\\ A & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we substitute the value of $A$ into $(1)$ to get the value of $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B & =3-7 \\\\ B & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\frac{7{x}^{2}-32x+42}{(x-2)^{3}}=\\frac{7}{x-2}-\\frac{4}{(x-2)^{2}}+\\frac{6}{(x-2)^{3}}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/state.json" "file_sha256" "a214c7f56d4a405e541980213466c5f921d158e09d5c1a7b15833d74a3eb6b65"} {"question" "q-351243" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0cc918ffd366d63cb92a1aec3422bc69dfe141ce7f8b052fa946427f57512019"} {"question" "q-351243" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/state.json" "file_sha256" "a214c7f56d4a405e541980213466c5f921d158e09d5c1a7b15833d74a3eb6b65"} {"question" "q-351243" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "7"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/state.json" "file_sha256" "a214c7f56d4a405e541980213466c5f921d158e09d5c1a7b15833d74a3eb6b65"} {"question" "q-351243" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/state.json" "file_sha256" "a214c7f56d4a405e541980213466c5f921d158e09d5c1a7b15833d74a3eb6b65"} {"question" "q-351243" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/state.json" "file_sha256" "a214c7f56d4a405e541980213466c5f921d158e09d5c1a7b15833d74a3eb6b65"} {"question" "q-351243" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/state.json" "file_sha256" "a214c7f56d4a405e541980213466c5f921d158e09d5c1a7b15833d74a3eb6b65"} {"question" "q-351243" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "6"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/state.json" "file_sha256" "a214c7f56d4a405e541980213466c5f921d158e09d5c1a7b15833d74a3eb6b65"} {"question" "q-69993" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that\n\n$$\n\\frac{1+3x}{(x-1)(x+1)^{3}}=\\frac{A}{x-1}+\\frac{B}{x+1}+\\frac{C}{(x+1)^{2}}+\\frac{D}{(x+1)^{3}},\n$$\n\nwhere $A$, $B$, $C$ and $D$ are real constants, find the value of $AB-CD.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/state.json" "file_sha256" "a214c7f56d4a405e541980213466c5f921d158e09d5c1a7b15833d74a3eb6b65"} {"question" "q-69993" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Multiplying both sides of the given equality by $(x-1)(x+1)^{3}$ gives\n\n$$\n1+3x=A(x+1)^{3}+B(x-1)(x+1)^{2}+C(x-1)(x+1)+D(x-1).\n$$\n\nLetting $x=-1$  gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1+3(-1) & =A(-1+1)^{3}+B(-1-1)(-1+1)^{2}+C(-1-1)(-1+1)+D(-1-1) \\\\ 1-3 & =-2D \\\\ -2 & =-2D \\\\ D & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=1$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1+3(1) & =A(1+1)^{3}+B(1-1)(1+1)^{2}+C(1-1)(1+1)+D(1-1) \\\\ 1+3 & =8A \\\\ 4 & =8A \\\\ A & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=0$ and using our values for $A$ and $D$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1+3(0) & =\\frac{1}{2}(0+1)^{3}+B(0-1)(0+1)^{2}+C(0-1)(0+1)+1(0-1) \\\\ 1 & =\\frac{1}{2}-B-C-1 \\\\ C & =-\\frac{3}{2}-B.\\,\\,(1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, letting $x=2$ and using our values for $A$ and $D$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1+3(2) & =\\frac{1}{2}(2+1)^{3}+B(2-1)(2+1)^{2}+C(2-1)(2+1)+1(2-1) \\\\ 1+6 & =\\frac{27}{2}+9B+3C+1 \\\\ 3C & =-\\frac{15}{2}-9B \\\\ C & =-\\frac{5}{2}-3B.\\,\\,(2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom $(1)$ and $(2)$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{2}-B & =-\\frac{5}{2}-3B \\\\ 2B & =-1 \\\\ B & =-\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we substitute the value of $B$ into $(1)$  to get the value of $C:$\n\n$$\nC=-\\frac{3}{2}-(-\\frac{1}{2})=-1\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\nAB-CD=\\frac{1}{2}(-\\frac{1}{2})-(-1)(1)=\\frac{3}{4}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/state.json" "file_sha256" "a214c7f56d4a405e541980213466c5f921d158e09d5c1a7b15833d74a3eb6b65"} {"question" "q-69993" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0cc918ffd366d63cb92a1aec3422bc69dfe141ce7f8b052fa946427f57512019"} {"question" "q-69993" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/state.json" "file_sha256" "a214c7f56d4a405e541980213466c5f921d158e09d5c1a7b15833d74a3eb6b65"} {"question" "q-69993" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{4}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/state.json" "file_sha256" "a214c7f56d4a405e541980213466c5f921d158e09d5c1a7b15833d74a3eb6b65"} {"question" "q-69993" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3}{4}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/state.json" "file_sha256" "a214c7f56d4a405e541980213466c5f921d158e09d5c1a7b15833d74a3eb6b65"} {"question" "e-12333" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that \n\n$$\n\\dfrac{7x+6}{(x+2)^2} = \\dfrac{A}{x+2} -\\dfrac{8}{(x+2)^2},\n$$\n\nwhat is the value of $A?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/example-12333.json" "file_sha256" "7e0d04563198b0389d62f4de754b0f811fd916749ca20435b956ae2915108f62"} {"question" "e-12333" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Multiplying both sides of the given equality by $(x+2)^2$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7x+6 & =A(x+2)-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can substitute some value for $x$ and solve for $A.$\n\nWe *can’t* choose $x=-2,$ since this would eliminate $A$ from the equation. But we can choose any other value of $x.$ So let’s choose a simple value, say, $x=0.$\n\nPlugging $x=0$ into the equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7x+6 & =A(x+2)-8 \\\\ 7(0)+6 & =A(0+2)-8 \\\\ 6 & =2A-8 \\\\ 14 & =2A \\\\ A & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/example-12333.json" "file_sha256" "7e0d04563198b0389d62f4de754b0f811fd916749ca20435b956ae2915108f62"} {"question" "e-12334" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that \n\n$$\n\\dfrac{7-4x}{(x+5)^2} = \\dfrac{A}{x+5} +\\dfrac{B}{(x+5)^2},\n$$\n\nfind the values of $A$ and $B.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/example-12334.json" "file_sha256" "427b7861b0c6474e7af2b33135a31a2a6eb2e9d2b5993a042fa003d392a89e70"} {"question" "e-12334" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Multiplying both sides of the given equality by $(x+5)^2$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7-4x & =A(x+5)+B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe want to solve for $A$ and $B,$ and both of these constants appear in the equation simultaneously. However, we can eliminate $A$ if we substitute $x=-5.$\n\nPlugging $x=-5$ into the equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7-4x & =A(x+5)+B \\\\ 7-4(-5) & =A(-5+5)+B \\\\ 27 & =A(0)+B \\\\ 27 & =0+B \\\\ 27 & =B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to solve for $A.$ To do this, let’s start by substituting our value $B=27$ into the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7-4x & =A(x+5)+27\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can substitute some value for $x$ and solve for $A.$\n\nWe *can’t* choose $x=-5,$ since this would eliminate $A$ from the equation. But we can choose any other value of $x.$ So let’s choose a simple value, say, $x=0.$\n\nPlugging $x=0$ into the equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7-4x & =A(x+5)+27 \\\\ 7-4(0) & =A(0+5)+27 \\\\ 7 & =5A+27 \\\\ -20 & =5A \\\\ A & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $A=-4$ and $B=27.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/example-12334.json" "file_sha256" "427b7861b0c6474e7af2b33135a31a2a6eb2e9d2b5993a042fa003d392a89e70"} {"question" "e-12335" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that \n\n$$\n\\dfrac{3x^2-5x+8}{(x-3)^2(x+1)} = \\dfrac{A}{(x-3)} +\\dfrac{B}{(x-3)^2} + \\dfrac{C}{(x+1)},\n$$\n\nwhere $A$, $B$, and $C$ are real constants, calculate $A\\cdot B\\cdot C.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/example-12335.json" "file_sha256" "c35bf4f703a59159b101a40498213ac9ff96862dcfe9b80eec63d4c184cc6da1"} {"question" "e-12335" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we multiply the expression through by $(x-3)^2(x+1)$ to give\n\n$$\n3x^2-5x+8= A(x-3)(x+1)+B(x+1)+C(x-3)^2.\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=3$ eliminates the $A$ and $C$ terms and allows us to solve for $B.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(3)^{2}-5(3)+8=B\\cdot 4\\,⟹\\,B=5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, plugging in $x=-1$ eliminates the $A$ and $B$ terms and allows us to solve for $C.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(-1)^{2}-5(-1)+8=C\\cdot (-4)^{2}\\,⟹\\,C=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUnfortunately, there is no value of $x$ that we can substitute to eliminate both $B$ and $C.$ However, using our results for $B$ and $C$ gives\n\n$$\n3x^2-5x+8= A(x-3)(x+1)+5(x+1)+1(x-3)^2,\n$$\n\nand we can plug in any value of $x$ to solve for $A.$ Let's choose the simplest number to plug in, $x=0.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8 & =A(0-3)(0+1)+5(0+1)+C(0-3)^{2} \\\\ 8 & =-3A+5+9 \\\\ -6 & =-3A \\\\ A & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nA\\cdot B\\cdot C=2\\cdot 5\\cdot 1=10,\n$$\n\nand the partial fraction decomposition is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{3x^2-5x+8}{(x-3)^2(x+1)} = \\dfrac{2}{(x-3)} +\\dfrac{5}{(x-3)^2} + \\dfrac{1}{(x+1)}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/example-12335.json" "file_sha256" "c35bf4f703a59159b101a40498213ac9ff96862dcfe9b80eec63d4c184cc6da1"} {"question" "e-12336" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1-2x}{(x+1)(x+2)^3}= \\dfrac{A}{x+1}+\\dfrac{B}{x+2} +\\dfrac{C}{(x+2)^2} + \\dfrac{D}{(x+2)^3},\n$$\n\nwhere $A$, $B$, $C$ and $D$ are real constants, determine the value of $AB + CD.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/example-12336.json" "file_sha256" "c70e7819d9f8f76d2c50b271513ec575e2d4bf54ea875a9944f54e9799c90cf3"} {"question" "e-12336" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Multiplying both sides of the given equality by $(x+1)(x+2)^3$ gives\n\n$$\n1 - 2x = A(x+2)^3 + B(x+1)(x+2)^2 + C(x+1)(x+2) + D(x+1).\n$$\n\nLetting $x = -2$  gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1-2(-2) & =A(-2+2)^{3}+B(-2+1)(-2+2)^{2}+C(-2+1)(-2+2)+D(-2+1) \\\\ 1+4 & =-D \\\\ D & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x = -1$  gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1-2(-1) & =A(-1+2)^{3}+B(-1+1)(-1+2)^{2}+C(-1+1)(-1+2)+D(-1+1) \\\\ 1+2 & =A \\\\ A & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x = 0$ and using our values for $A$ and $D$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1-2(0) & =3(0+2)^{3}+B(0+1)(0+2)^{2}+C(0+1)(0+2)+(-5)(0+1) \\\\ 1-0 & =24+4B+2C-5 \\\\ 2C & =-4B-18 \\\\ C & =-2B-9.\\,\\,(1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, letting $x = 1$ and using our values for $A$ and $D$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1-2(1) & =A(1+2)^{3}+B(1+1)(1+2)^{2}+C(1+1)(1+2)+D(1+1) \\\\ 1-2 & =81+18B+6C-10 \\\\ 6C & =-18B-72 \\\\ C & =-3B-12.\\,\\,(2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom $(1)$ and $(2)$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2B-9 & =-3B-12 \\\\ B & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we substitute the value of $B$ into $(1)$  to get the value of $C{:}$\n\n$$\nC = -2(-3) - 9 = -3\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\nAB + CD = 3(-3) + (-3)(-5) = 6.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038618/example-12336.json" "file_sha256" "c70e7819d9f8f76d2c50b271513ec575e2d4bf54ea875a9944f54e9799c90cf3"}] "usage" {"e-12335" [] "q-51141" [] "e-12336" [] "q-115105" [] "q-351243" [] "e-12333" [] "q-73204" [] "e-12334" []} "basis" 1318 "retractions" [[17592186097268 :question/problem "Given that\n$(x + 8)/((x - 2)^{2}) = \\frac{A}{x - 2} + (B)/((x - 2)^{2})$,\n\nwhere $A$ and $B$ are real constants, what is the value of $A \\cdot B$?"] [17592186096307 :question/problem "Given that\n$\\dfrac{7x+6}{(x+2)^2} = \\dfrac{A}{x+2} -\\dfrac{8}{(x+2)^2}$,\n\nwhat is the value of $A$?"] [17592186096307 :question/worked-solution "Multiplying both sides of the given equality by $(x+2)^2$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n7x + 6 &= A(x + 2) - 8\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can substitute some value for $x$ and solve for $A$.\n\nWe *can’t* choose $x=-2$, since this would eliminate $A$ from the equation. But we can choose any other value of $x$. So let’s choose a simple value, say, $x=0$.\n\nPlugging $x=0$ into the equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n7x + 6 &= A(x + 2) - 8 \\\\\n7(0) + 6 &= A(0 + 2) - 8 \\\\\n6 &= 2A - 8 \\\\\n14 &= 2A \\\\\nA &= 7\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186096308 :question/problem "Given that\n$\\dfrac{7-4x}{(x+5)^2} = \\dfrac{A}{x+5} +\\dfrac{B}{(x+5)^2}$,\n\nfind the values of $A$ and $B$."] [17592186096308 :question/worked-solution "Multiplying both sides of the given equality by $(x+5)^2$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n7 - 4x &= A(x + 5) + B\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe want to solve for $A$ and $B$, and both of these constants appear in the equation simultaneously. However, we can eliminate $A$ if we substitute $x=-5$.\n\nPlugging $x=-5$ into the equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n7 - 4x &= A(x + 5) + B \\\\\n7 - 4(-5) &= A(-5 + 5) + B \\\\\n27 &= A(0) + B \\\\\n27 &= 0 + B \\\\\n27 &= B\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to solve for $A$. To do this, let’s start by substituting our value $B=27$ into the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n7 - 4x &= A(x + 5) + 27\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can substitute some value for $x$ and solve for $A$.\n\nWe *can’t* choose $x=-5$, since this would eliminate $A$ from the equation. But we can choose any other value of $x$. So let’s choose a simple value, say, $x=0$.\n\nPlugging $x=0$ into the equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n7 - 4x &= A(x + 5) + 27 \\\\\n7 - 4(0) &= A(0 + 5) + 27 \\\\\n7 &= 5A + 27 \\\\\n- 20 &= 5A \\\\\nA &= -4\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $A=-4$ and $B=27$."] [17592186096309 :question/problem "Given that\n$\\dfrac{3x^2-5x+8}{(x-3)^2(x+1)} = \\dfrac{A}{(x-3)} +\\dfrac{B}{(x-3)^2} + \\dfrac{C}{(x+1)}$,\nwhere $A$, $B$, and $C$ are real constants, calculate $A\\cdot B\\cdot C$."] [17592186096309 :question/worked-solution "First, we multiply the expression through by $(x-3)^2(x+1)$ to give\n\n$$\n3x^2-5x+8= A(x-3)(x+1)+B(x+1)+C(x-3)^2\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=3$ eliminates the $A$ and $C$ terms and allows us to solve for $B$. We get\n\n$$\n3(3)^{2} - 5(3) + 8 = B \\cdot 4⟹B = 5\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, plugging in $x=-1$ eliminates the $A$ and $B$ terms and allows us to solve for $C$. We get\n\n$$\n3(-1)^{2} - 5(-1) + 8 = C \\cdot (-4)^{2}⟹C = 1\n$$\n\nUnfortunately, there is no value of $x$ that we can substitute to eliminate both $B$ and $C$. However, using our results for $B$ and $C$ gives\n\n$$\n3x^2-5x+8= A(x-3)(x+1)+5(x+1)+1(x-3)^2\n$$\n\nand we can plug in any value of $x$ to solve for $A$. Let's choose the simplest number to plug in, $x=0$. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n8 &= A(0 - 3)(0 + 1) + 5(0 + 1) + C(0 - 3)^{2} \\\\\n8 &= -3A + 5 + 9 \\\\\n- 6 &= -3A \\\\\nA &= 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nA\\cdot B\\cdot C=2\\cdot 5\\cdot 1=10\n$$\n\nand the partial fraction decomposition is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{3x^2-5x+8}{(x-3)^2(x+1)} = \\dfrac{2}{(x-3)} +\\dfrac{5}{(x-3)^2} + \\dfrac{1}{(x+1)}\n$$"] [17592186096310 :question/problem "Given that\n\n$\\dfrac{1-2x}{(x+1)(x+2)^3}= \\dfrac{A}{x+1}+\\dfrac{B}{x+2} +\\dfrac{C}{(x+2)^2} + \\dfrac{D}{(x+2)^3}$,\n\nwhere $A$, $B$, $C$ and $D$ are real constants, determine the value of $AB + CD$."] [17592186096310 :question/worked-solution "Multiplying both sides of the given equality by $(x+1)(x+2)^3$ gives\n\n$$\n1 - 2x = A(x+2)^3 + B(x+1)(x+2)^2 + C(x+1)(x+2) + D(x+1)\n$$\n\nLetting $x = -2$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n1 - 2(-2) &= A(-2 + 2)^{3} + B(-2 + 1)(-2 + 2)^{2} + C(-2 + 1)(-2 + 2) + D(-2 + 1) \\\\\n1 + 4 &= -D \\\\\nD &= -5\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x = -1$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n1 - 2(-1) &= A(-1 + 2)^{3} + B(-1 + 1)(-1 + 2)^{2} + C(-1 + 1)(-1 + 2) + D(-1 + 1) \\\\\n1 + 2 &= A \\\\\nA &= 3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x = 0$ and using our values for $A$ and $D$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n1 - 2(0) &= 3(0 + 2)^{3} + B(0 + 1)(0 + 2)^{2} + C(0 + 1)(0 + 2) + (-5)(0 + 1) \\\\\n1 - 0 &= 24 + 4B + 2C - 5 \\\\\n2C &= -4B - 18 \\\\\nC &= -2B - 9.(1)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, letting $x = 1$ and using our values for $A$ and $D$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n1 - 2(1) &= A(1 + 2)^{3} + B(1 + 1)(1 + 2)^{2} + C(1 + 1)(1 + 2) + D(1 + 1) \\\\\n1 - 2 &= 81 + 18B + 6C - 10 \\\\\n6C &= -18B - 72 \\\\\nC &= -3B - 12.(2)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom $(1)$ and $(2)$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-2B - 9 &= -3B - 12 \\\\\nB &= -3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we substitute the value of $B$ into $(1)$ to get the value of $C{:}$\n\n$$\nC = -2(-3) - 9 = -3\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\nAB + CD = 3(-3) + (-3)(-5) = 6\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186095966 17592186095967 17592186095968 17592186095969 17592186095970 17592186266345 17592186266346 17592186266347 17592186266348 17592186266349 17592186266402 17592186266404 17592186266406 17592186266409 17592186266410 17592186266411 17592186266412 17592186266413] "immutable_fields" [[17592186095965 :answer-field/correct] [17592186095965 :answer-field/id] [17592186095965 :answer-field/key] [17592186095965 :answer-field/type] [17592186266344 :answer-field/correct] [17592186266344 :answer-field/id] [17592186266344 :answer-field/key] [17592186266344 :answer-field/type] [17592186266401 :answer-field/correct] [17592186266401 :answer-field/id] [17592186266401 :answer-field/key] [17592186266401 :answer-field/type] [17592186266403 :answer-field/correct] [17592186266403 :answer-field/id] [17592186266403 :answer-field/key] [17592186266403 :answer-field/type] [17592186266405 :answer-field/correct] [17592186266405 :answer-field/id] [17592186266405 :answer-field/key] [17592186266405 :answer-field/type] [17592186266408 :answer-field/correct] [17592186266408 :answer-field/id] [17592186266408 :answer-field/key] [17592186266408 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
